      "text": "1. Embedding",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 18,
      "containerId": "v2L231yqdOGaMujv1KMGp",
      "originalText": "1. Embedding",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VZsqqb_33V7y3RaN-FNCO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 604.6507936507929,
      "y": 2654.015873015876,
      "width": 749.7195434570312,
      "height": 1425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 38326910,
      "version": 2248,
      "versionNonce": 767166398,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791837087906,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "/pipeline \n1. upload : handle by api\n2. parse \n    parse based on doc type\n    - lazy load dependency\n    - pdfplumber/unstructured \n    - doc\n        - paragraph\n        - table\n            - extract cells\n        - heading\n            - find level (style name)\n        - list_item\n            - ./-/1,2,3\n        return Block  \n3. clean\n    - remove footprint/disclosure/page number\n    - remove extra white space  \n4. chunk -> {section_path, title, content, cnt, metadata}\n    - Re: define keywords eg (1-9, chapter, session, etc.)\n    - chunk(ParsedDoc): chunk based on blocks \n        - sections:\n            - seperate into section by headings\n                - use a stack to track heading level \n                    - pop when level < len(stack) \n            - return {path, title, blocks, page} \n        - for each section:\n            - params: units, chunks, buf, buf_len, page\n            - flush()\n                - split_untis(blocks): list[tuple[str, int, bool]]\n                    - split chunks into units\n                        - split lines \n                            - one paragraph could have many clause \n                            - split by clause_re (pattern)\n                            - if too granular, keep the original line \n        \n        \n5. extract metadata\n    - use LLM to extract keywords and other metadata\n6. vector + 7. index. index.py\n    - init: store, vector_store, embeddingClient, bm25Index, llm + above \n    - ingest process \n        1. check doc duplicated? - by hash document\n        2. parse + clean + chunk + get metadata\n        3. find the latest title (same doc in dept)\n        4. insert into document table \n            - set vector status to pending  \n        5. vectorize\n            1.  extract content from chunk \n            2. embedding \n        6. indexing, vector + bm 25\n                - vectors[i]\n                - chunks[i]\n                - insert (chunk_id, vector[i]) into vector db\n                - insert chunk_doc (chunk_id, all metadata, content) to db\n                - update status to ready \n8. extract cross depts",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 1418,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "/pipeline \n1. upload : handle by api\n2. parse \n    parse based on doc type\n    - lazy load dependency\n    - pdfplumber/unstructured \n    - doc\n        - paragraph\n        - table\n            - extract cells\n        - heading\n            - find level (style name)\n        - list_item\n            - ./-/1,2,3\n        return Block  \n3. clean\n    - remove footprint/disclosure/page number\n    - remove extra white space  \n4. chunk -> {section_path, title, content, cnt, metadata}\n    - Re: define keywords eg (1-9, chapter, session, etc.)\n    - chunk(ParsedDoc): chunk based on blocks \n        - sections:\n            - seperate into section by headings\n                - use a stack to track heading level \n                    - pop when level < len(stack) \n            - return {path, title, blocks, page} \n        - for each section:\n            - params: units, chunks, buf, buf_len, page\n            - flush()\n                - split_untis(blocks): list[tuple[str, int, bool]]\n                    - split chunks into units\n                        - split lines \n                            - one paragraph could have many clause \n                            - split by clause_re (pattern)\n                            - if too granular, keep the original line \n        \n        \n5. extract metadata\n    - use LLM to extract keywords and other metadata\n6. vector + 7. index. index.py\n    - init: store, vector_store, embeddingClient, bm25Index, llm + above \n    - ingest process \n        1. check doc duplicated? - by hash document\n        2. parse + clean + chunk + get metadata\n        3. find the latest title (same doc in dept)\n        4. insert into document table \n            - set vector status to pending  \n        5. vectorize\n            1.  extract content from chunk \n            2. embedding \n        6. indexing, vector + bm 25\n                - vectors[i]\n                - chunks[i]\n                - insert (chunk_id, vector[i]) into vector db\n                - insert chunk_doc (chunk_id, all metadata, content) to db\n                - update status to ready \n8. extract cross depts",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
